{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 57, :comments ["<b>This is the law of tzara'at.</b> One must not add and stringently render tamei other skin afflictions, even though among us there are many types of tzara'at besides these, as it says: אַל תּוֹסְףּ עַל דְּבָרָיו (Proverbs 30:6). For despite their severity, they are not judged by the law of tzara'at at all — as Scripture declared pure when the affliction turned entirely white, having passed beyond the boundary of tamei tzara'at toward the worse, like the manner of burned impurity whose form has been destroyed."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:18.015555853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}